= A Meeting in a Beer Hall

[? if bavaria_soviet = 2 : On 24 February, in a Nuremberg beer hall full of officers and students who fled red Munich, ?][? if bavaria_soviet != 2 : On 24 February, in the great hall of the Hofbräuhaus in Munich, ?] the little German Workers' Party holds its biggest meeting yet. A former corporal named Adolf Hitler reads out twenty-five points: against Versailles, against "interest slavery", against the Jews. A week later the party renames itself the National Socialist German Workers' Party.

Our Munich comrades send a short report.

- @file: File it with the other reports on the Bavarian leagues.
- @meetings: Send the youth to break up their meetings.

@file
subtitle: There are a dozen such leagues in Bavaria.

The report goes into a drawer at the Zentrale.

@meetings
subtitle: Brawls in the beer halls. The police will take names.
on-arrival: militancy += 3; lean_offensive += 1

Our young comrades turn up at the meetings in groups. The Nazis answer with a "hall protection" squad of former soldiers.
